  "scientific_summary": "r538 one author-complete candidate, not claimed as qualified. 353552 list color function threshold: for m >= 4 and 2l <= (m-1)^2 every m-assignment of K_{2,l} has at least P(K_{2,l},m) proper colorings, so tau(K_{2,l}) <= max(4, ceil(1+sqrt(2l))), which with source Theorem 4 settles Conjecture 5; the author also gets the limit of tau/sqrt(l). The follow-up paper proves the two easy cases and says a proof will require a novel refinement or an entirely new approach. Routed to independent adversarial qualification. 344764 printed bound is false at small n by a table of the work the source attributes it to, a public correction, zero. 360343 appears to be a transcription defect, zero. 359433 and 373534 source-own. Fifteen parked. Credit 0, 58/80.",
